  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3160 (head 5e7c2b0d0). Work this issue after that PR merges.\n\n1. A machine file under an existing session name replaces the stored text with no message. A post file in the same case is refused. The posted program does not change, because the project holds the parsed machine. But the catalogue and Edit then show a text that differs from the mounted machine. Refuse different machine text under an existing name, as for posts.\n2. The lists do not show which post or machine is a session file. A session file `grbl.cps` shows next to the shipped post `grbl`. Add a mark in plain English, for example \"(this session)\".\n3. No test covers the same-name case for the drop on the setup page. The folder pick and the single pick have a test.\n4. A single Load machine or Load post pick is bounded before the read only by the limit of 256 MiB for each file. The 32 MiB check comes after the bytes are in memory. Check the size before the read, as the batch reads do.\n5. Nothing compiles the wasm32 build of `camcraft-ui` in a gate. The browser-only code of PR #3160 is behind `cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")` and was not compiled. Add a check step, or record why not.\n",
